$MDESC::Type = "CTF_HamstersMaps";
$MDESC::Text = "<s3><f1>Mission Type: <f0> Capture the Flag" @
         "\n<f1>Author: <f0> Hamster_of_Doom!" @
	 "\n<f1>Questions, Comments, Pity: <f0> rvr279@home.com" @
 	 "\n<f1>ICQ: <f0> 25400277 <f1>AIM: <f0> Rover v1" @	 
	 "\n<f1>Map Version: <f0> 1.0" @
	 "\n<f1>Updates: <f0> http://members.home.net/rvr279/hamster" @
	 "\n<f1>Map Type: <f0> Server-Side" @
	 "\n<f1>Planet: <f0> Talus XXI" @
         "\n<f1>System: <f0> Talus" @
         "\n<f1>Gravity: <f0> Normal" @ 
	 "\n<f1>Weather: <f0> Cloudy" @
         "\n<f1>Time of Day: <f0> Midday" @ 
         "\n<f1>Date: <f0> August 29th, 4001" @
         "\n<f1>Campaign: <f0> Phoenix Rising" @         
	 "\n<f1># of Captures to Victory: <f0> 15" @
	 "\n<f1># of Teams: <f0> 2" @
	 "\n<f1>Max # of Players: <f0> 20" @
         "\n\n<f1>Briefing:<f0> Listen up soldiers! Since the battle of Omikidd ended in a near total draw, the Tribal laws delegate that we the participants select their strongest soldiers and send them to a battleground. Since you are our elite veterans, I don't have to tell you that the laws state that this trial battle be to the death. That is why you are here today. Our hated enemy will be sending in their best. There is nothing before this battle and nothing beyond until one side emerges in victory! I know fate has ordained our clan to emerge the victors, because she has allowed your survival, perhaps for this battle. Though I can not yet disclose to you the tactical reasons this victory is necessary, you already know your own reasons why you will win this battle.\n\nFailure is not an option.\n\nDISMISSED!\n\n<f1>Tips:\n<f0>Each base has a healer that will recover all health instantly.\nRemember, force-fields don't protect you from explosive fire.\nDon't jam your doors open.\nThere are no exposed generators.\nThe high ground can be advantageous\n\n<f1>Thanks to:\n<f0>Shadow of Death and Tedaw for debuting my maps on their server!\nOmnipotent & others for their mapping tutorials.\nThe mapping community at large for inspiration, demonstration, and perspiration.\nAnd of course the team at Dynamix for Tribes!";
